ground_truth:
The solution involves key changes in four files:

1.  **`config/app_config.ini`:**
    ```ini
    [RoutingRules]
    # Maps X-Service-Version header values to backend URLs
    beta = http://127.0.0.1:8081
    alpha = http://127.0.0.1:8082
    ```

2.  **`src/app_context.h`:**
    ```c
    // In AppContext struct definition
    HashTable* routing_rules; // Stores version-to-URL routing map
    ```

3.  **`src/main.c`:**
    ```c
    // Inside the configuration loading function
    // ... after loading other configs ...
    context->routing_rules = ht_create();
    // Example parsing logic (implementation depends on INI parser used)
    // ini_browse with a callback to populate the hash table from [RoutingRules]
    // for each key, value in section:
    //   ht_set(context->routing_rules, key, value);
    ```

4.  **`src/adapters/rest_handler.c`:**
    ```c
    // Inside the main request handling function
    const char* default_backend_url = app_context->config.backend_url;
    const char* target_backend_url = default_backend_url;

    const char* version_header = get_request_header(request, "X-Service-Version");
    if (version_header != NULL) {
        const char* mapped_url = ht_get(app_context->routing_rules, version_header);
        if (mapped_url != NULL) {
            target_backend_url = mapped_url;
            log_info("Routing request to versioned backend: %s", version_header);
        } else {
            log_info("Version '%s' not found in routing rules, using default backend.", version_header);
        }
    } else {
        log_info("No version header found, using default backend.");
    }

    // ... use target_backend_url in the subsequent proxying logic (e.g., curl_easy_setopt)
    ```

5.  **`docs/OpenAPI.yaml`:**
    ```yaml
    # ... inside components ...
    components:
      parameters:
        ServiceVersionHeader:
          name: X-Service-Version
          in: header
          description: >
            Directs the request to a specific version of the backend service. 
            If omitted, the request is routed to the default stable service.
          required: false
          schema:
            type: string
            example: "beta"

    # ... inside a path definition ...
    paths:
      /some/endpoint:
        get:
          summary: Retrieves some data
          parameters:
            - $ref: '#/components/parameters/ServiceVersionHeader'
          responses:
            '200':
              description: OK
    ```
